Package: com.qingc12.pullovermf
Name: PullOverMF
Version: 0.1.5
Architecture: iphoneos-arm64e
Description: MultiFloat personal fork of PullOver X (GPL-3.0). Floating multitask window / split view for iOS 14+ (roothide / arm64e). 0.1.5: ring picker geometry fix - the dial centre is now inset from the screen edge (screenWidth - radius - mfRingEdgeMargin) so the WHOLE circle is visible inside the screen instead of being cut in half; icons are arranged around the full 360-degree circle starting from the top (mfRingStartAngle) and the default icon size is reduced from 56 to 44pt (mfRingIconSize). New options: mfRingEdgeMargin (12), mfRingStartAngle (-90). 0.1.4: critical link fix - 0.1.2/0.1.3 failed to load entirely because PullOverX.mm is ObjC++ and called cross-file C functions declared without extern "C" (mangled refs __Z9MFLogRawCPKc / __Z19MFRingPickerInstallv could not be resolved by dyld, so the whole dylib was rejected: no handle, no log file). All shared C interfaces are now wrapped in extern "C". 0.1.3: Stheno-style ring picker summoned by a configurable edge-gesture strip (verified working above a full-screen app), tap an icon to open that app in the float, long-press to remove it (ringApps); plus pure-C MFLogRawC() file logging to /var/mobile/PullOverMF.log.
Maintainer: QingC12
Author: PullOver X by mlgm / PullOver Pro by c1d3rDev / fork by QingC12 <QingC12@users.noreply.github.com>
Section: Tweaks
Depends: firmware (>= 14.0)
Priority: optional
